// The Phase 1 mission (ADR-0201 §9): the vertical slice — one mission on
// crossroads_64 with the unchanged Legion content. The objective set is the
// two kinds the slice proves: destroy the enemy (required) and grow the
// workforce to eight (optional). No AI settings, no restrictions — those are
// later Phase 2 packages; no campaign file — that is Phase 3.
//
// Schema version 2 (Phase 2, ADR-0201 §3): the fog preset. This mission
// declares the default — today's all-Hidden init, byte-for-byte — which
// encodes to the exact Phase 1 mission id (the encoder's extension rule:
// a default preset appends no bytes), so the mission's identity is
// unchanged by the declaration.
//
// The optional objective's count is authored above the Legion starting
// force (1 command center + 4 workers per player, plan §9.7): the owner
// ruled (2026-10-16, the audit's AUD-003) that BuildTrain keeps its
// "N exist" existence semantics — counting currently owned entities,
// starting units included — so the target must exceed the starting four
// for the objective to mean anything ("grow to 8 workers"). The starting
// 200 ore is exactly four workers' cost, so the goal is reachable by
// pure production from the opening economy.
(
    schema_version: 2,
    id: "crossroads_01",
    display_name: "Crossroads",
    map: "crossroads_64",
    faction: "legion",
    rules: "alpha",
    fog_preset: Default,
    objectives: [
        // Destroy the enemy command center — a surgical target distinct from
        // the elimination rule, proving the objective model's expressiveness.
        (
            kind: "Destroy",
            parameters: Destroy(( target_kind: Some("command_center") )),
            optional: false,
        ),
        // Grow the workforce to eight workers — optional: it feeds the end
        // screen and the story hooks, never the match outcome. The count is
        // current ownership ("N exist"), so it must sit above the starting
        // four to require any play at all (AUD-003); the starting ore funds
        // exactly the four missing workers.
        (
            kind: "BuildTrain",
            parameters: BuildTrain(( kind: "worker", count: 8 )),
            optional: true,
        ),
    ],
)
